  "briefing": {
    "situation": "Dumbo in the Gulf (5 November, night). You fly a PBY-5A from the lit San Pedro Bay anchorage to find a downed fighter pilot's raft in the search area to the southeast, about seven miles out. Land on the water within 150 yards of the raft, ease up to it and stay slower than two knots for twenty seconds while three men climb aboard, then take off and bring them home to the anchorage. A fourth man is adrift a short taxi from the raft: take him aboard too, if you can. Two Japanese fighters may pass at a distance once the first men are aboard. This is a composite mission: no specific documented rescue is reenacted. Water landings at night are hard: the approach and touchdown are yours to judge.",
    "loadout": "clean"
  },
  "history": {
    "text": "Task Force 77's Operation Plan 13-44 coordinated the rescue of downed aviators in Leyte Gulf and used PBY flying boats, with seaplane tenders, where it was practical; PBYs of the Navy's patrol squadrons operated from the gulf with tender support through the campaign. This mission is a composite inspired by that work, written for the game, and is not a reconstruction of any documented rescue: the crew, the night, the raft and the pilot are invented.",
    "sources": [
      "Task Force 77, Operation Plan 13-44, Annex G (air-sea rescue): https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/USN/rep/Leyte/OpPlan/13-44-G.html",
      "Dictionary of American Naval Aviation Squadrons, vol. 2, VPB-33: https://www.history.navy.mil/content/dam/nhhc/research/histories/naval-aviation/dictionary-of-american-naval-aviation-squadrons-volume-2/pdfs/chap4-3.pdf"
    ]
  }
